flooding continues along the river seven  pushing water into communities built  along its banks after a barrage of  storms a truly destructive force  oh god i haven't even been in here  okay oh  siobhan connor shows us around her  family home in shrewsbury  it has been flooded 17 times in the last  25 years i think people don't realize  until you're in this you know it's not a  case of  getting some flash and cleaning you know  it really is  this is  sewage you know this is over spilled i  mean look at the color of it this is  toilet water you know you know that  we're stood in and it's in your home  she is exhausted and angry  how can you kind of where do you start  figuring out where the water comes from  when you've done everything you can to  mitigate flooding and to protect your  home i mean it's just heartbreaking  in nearby bewdley emergency workers  check on houses next to temporary  barriers that didn't hold the water back  scientists have warned that flood risks  are increasing as climate change drives  more frequent and intense rainfall it  makes these permanent barriers which  held firm on the other side of the river  even more important  that's why the government's recently  announced a 5 billion pound national  flood defense strategy to help build  more things like this to help  communities adapt but the blunt truth is  that they can't possibly hold back all  the water or protect everyone's homes  the environment agency knows things are  not going to get easier it's always very  worrying especially when you get named  storms one after the other we've seen  some record levels on our gauging  stations up in the top of the river  seven when i first started 20 years ago  this would have been you know one in a  career event and i've had three in the  last three years  up and down this river it may be days  before the waters recede and the lengthy  and expensive cleanup begins but they  will come again and again potentially an  increasingly common feature of our  warming world  hannah thomas peter sky news imbuedly
 

